# S46a-track: S46a-held's window as the models' wireframe on black at 960x540: where the
# grunt is in each frame, for the crop that follows it.
#
# Assembly (S46a): a 470x520 crop that follows the grunt, enlarged 2x (nearest), from
# S46a-held at (13,20) and S46a-blended at (967,20) of a black 1920x1080 frame, each film
# frame shown twice, labelled "poses held (id's)" and "poses blended (slop)". The crop's
# centre: S46a-track draws only the moving models' wireframe on black; each frame's lit
# pixels, less those lit in most frames, give the grunt's centre (scaled to 1080p), and a
# cubic fitted through the centres over the window is the crop's path. (Today `camera
# follow monster_army#N` does such a follow in the engine.)

map e1m1
wake 0,576,24 at 0

duration 13.3
fps 30
size 960x540
frames 114..397

preset slop
speed 0.125
hud off
player 190,616,24,190
cvar gamma 0.8

camera fixed 190,616,46 2,200

xray black
wire entities through

sound off
events on
